    "id": "p15-q17-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following. $\\frac{2x^2-6x}{(x+2)^2}\\times\\frac{5x+10}{x-2}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{10x(x-3)}{(x+2)(x-2)}$, $x\\ne-2,2$.\n\nFactorise both numerators and cancel one factor of $x+2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2x^2-6x}{(x+2)^2}\\times\\frac{5x+10}{x-2}&=\\frac{2x(x-3)}{(x+2)^2}\\times\\frac{5(x+2)}{x-2}\\\\\\frac{2x^2-6x}{(x+2)^2}\\times\\frac{5x+10}{x-2}&=\\frac{10x(x-3)}{(x+2)(x-2)}\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: $x\\ne-2,2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 30
  },
